AI Usage Disclosure
AI tool used
ChatGPT (OpenAI) was used as a development assistant during the School Admission System assignment.
Areas where AI assistance was used
- Interpreting the assignment requirements and breaking them into implementation steps.
- Planning the ASP.NET Core, React, PostgreSQL, and Docker Compose structure.
- Drafting and refining example backend and frontend code, including API integration and user interface behavior.
- Troubleshooting local development issues involving Visual Studio, Git, Docker Desktop, WSL, and Docker Compose.
- Preparing documentation and manual verification steps.
Review and verification
AI-generated suggestions were incorporated into the project and checked through local development and Docker execution. The frontend, backend, and PostgreSQL services were observed running in Docker, and the class-list API returned a successful response. The application was also checked through its browser interface.

Limitations of verification: Running containers and manual UI checks do not, by themselves, prove every edge case. Automated backend tests, including the required concurrent seat-reservation test, should be run and their results documented before final submission. This document does not claim that unverified tests passed.
Responsibility and corrections
The developer is responsible for reviewing, adapting, testing, and submitting the final implementation. AI suggestions may contain errors or omit requirements; they should be checked against the assignment and actual application behavior. Any corrections made during testing should be committed to the repository.
